# Supabase Access Control

- New publishing and minting tables must ship with an explicit access-control strategy before UI code depends on them.
- Prefer server-mediated writes or clearly defined RLS policies over front-end ownership checks alone.
- Keep schema changes additive and backwards-compatible while legacy novel flows still exist.
- Public reads should expose only approved and published content metadata.
- Review-only, draft, and staging assets must not become anonymously writable or publicly readable by accident.
- Treat service-role usage as backend-only and never leak privileged credentials into the client app.
